## Recommended next: Direction E — Xendit-for-guests refactor (T2 ~18-25K)

Logical continuation of Direction A. Customer chooses "Pay with Xendit" on checkout →
order created + Xendit invoice created in same transaction → client redirects to
Xendit payment URL. Currently impossible because createXenditInvoice is writeProcedure
(protected) — guests cannot call it.

Scope:
- NEW: `apps/web/src/lib/xendit-invoice.ts` (server-only helper `createXenditInvoiceForOrder`
  — extract the Xendit-call logic from the existing createXenditInvoice writeProcedure body;
  accepts {orderId, order, tenant} and returns {invoiceId, invoiceUrl}; throws TRPCError on
  Xendit-side failure so callers can roll back the surrounding transaction).
- MOD: `apps/web/src/server/trpc/routers/storefront.ts`
  - Refactor `createXenditInvoice` writeProcedure to call the new helper (no behavior change).
  - Extend `placeOrderAsCustomerInputSchema.paymentMethod` enum to include `"xendit"`.
  - When paymentMethod="xendit": inside the existing $transaction, after order creation,
    call createXenditInvoiceForOrder + persist xenditPaymentId on the created order.
  - Return shape becomes `{orderId, orderNumber, invoiceUrl?: string}` (invoiceUrl present
    only on xendit path).
- MOD: `apps/web/src/app/(tenant)/[slug]/store/checkout/checkout-form.tsx`
  - Add 3rd radio option "Pay online via Xendit" to PaymentMethod.
  - onSuccess: if `data.invoiceUrl` present → redirect to invoiceUrl (not to /products);
    else keep existing redirect behavior.
- MOD: `apps/web/src/__tests__/storefront.test.ts`
  - 3 new tests under placeOrderAsCustomer describe: (1) xendit happy path creates invoice
    + persists xenditPaymentId + returns invoiceUrl, (2) Xendit-side failure rolls back the
    order via transaction (no order row + no stock movement), (3) paymentMethod="xendit" with
    missing TenantXenditConfig rejects gracefully.
  - 2 new tests under existing createXenditInvoice describe verifying the refactor preserves
    current behavior (no regression).

Branch: feat/batch-20-xendit-for-guests
RED→GREEN: write all 5 new tests first, confirm RED, then write helper + refactor.

