## Standing 9-point pre-flight (run before any code on any batch)

1. `git status` + `git log -1` — confirm tree state.
2. `pnpm vitest run` — confirm 692/692 GREEN baseline.
3. Read input Zod schema of any router procedure the batch claims to reuse.
4. If router newly READS a field, verify all existing tests on that path mock the field.
5. Grep schema.prisma for any model in scope; confirm fields before scoping migrations.
6. Confirm package.json has any third-party library called out in scope.
7. Re-read .claude/rules/memory-governance.md §1 for the tier classification.
8. Emit explicit branch-creation line item in the BUILD BATCH PROPOSAL.
9. For publicProcedure vs protectedProcedure claims, grep the router to verify.

## Recurring-pattern lessons banked (apply at next batch PRE-FLIGHT)

- 🟢 publicProcedure tenant resolution — input.tenantSlug → db.tenant.findUnique; default
  warehouse resolved server-side. NEVER let client supply warehouseId on a public path.
- 🟢 System-actor lookup for guest writes — db.user.findFirst({isActive:true},
  orderBy:{createdAt:"asc"}) → returns seeded webmaster for required createdById FKs.
- 🟢 Rate-limit tier — rateLimiters.public.check(ip) at 30/min/IP for guest mutations.
- 🟢 sanitizePlainText on user-facing text fields (firstName/lastName/notes) before storage.
- ⚖️ Order-creation duplication tolerated — extraction deferred until 3rd variant emerges.
- 🔴 useCart() shape gotcha — destructure mismatch caught at typecheck. ALWAYS grep the
  CartContextValue's useMemo value before destructuring in a new consumer.
- 🟢 Intentional scope-trim — 2× consecutive (Item 1 cart-only, Item 2 order-only). When a
  Direction touches a new security/integration surface, ship that surface in its own batch.

## Trigger
Say "start Phase 8 Batch 20" or "start Direction E" — agent reads STATE.md first, runs the
9-point pre-flight, then emits BUILD BATCH PROPOSAL with explicit branch-creation line.
